 - **Assistant ("ask creaite", ⌘J / Ctrl+J or the floating button):** the live server runs Claude Code headless in this vault (`claude -p … --output-format stream-json`, resuming the session ID) so the same CLAUDE.md, skills, settings and permission rules apply. Headless runs cannot ask for permission, so tools are limited by `.claude/settings.json` plus a strict allow list; anything that changes the record (apply, undo, proposals, drafting reports) is confirmed by Alan in the chat panel first, and file changes follow BL-141. A request runs until it finishes or Alan presses Stop: closing the panel or the page doesn't stop it (the page reattaches), one runs at a time, and an unwatched run ends after `assistant.run_timeout_minutes`. Alan can paste, drop or attach up to four PNG or JPEG images (BL-100): they are for discussion only, nothing is extracted from them, and they are deleted with their chat. Never use a skip-permissions mode. **Reading is open, all the time (Alan, 2026-10-09):** every Microsoft 365 reading tool (calendar, mail search, Teams chats and channels, SharePoint and OneDrive search, people, and `read_resource`, which reads events, chats and meeting transcripts), every vault and project file, and every creaite script's read commands, with no prompt; **Microsoft 365 actions stay off** (sending, deleting or changing mail, calendar, Teams or files act outside the laptop and can't be undone), and changes follow BL-141. The lists are `READ_TOOLS` and `DENY_TOOLS` in `live_server.py`, built from `permissions.M365_READ` and `M365_ACTIONS`, and doctor treats a reading rule as normal but flags an action rule or the whole connector. It reads the vault, the projects root and the home folder (`--add-dir`), minus the never list, and changes files only through `filechange.py` (BL-141).
 - **AI on selected text (BL-301 D):** in any editor, a selection's **AI ▾** menu (or Alt+/) asks for a suggestion through `POST /api/edit/ai` (token-checked). `edit_ai.py` builds the prompt from the selected text, the option and the project's name, people and open item IDs only; Claude runs as the run kind `edit-ai` with **no tools at all** (`--tools ""`, `--strict-mcp-config`, an empty allow list, no `--add-dir`), so it cannot read a file or mail, run anything or write. The reply is a suggestion with BL-106's plain-code check under it; nothing changes until Alan accepts it (one undoable edit), a one-line field stays one line, a confidential text asks once first, and only counts go to `draft-stats.json` (feature `edit`); the debug log gets the option, place and length, never text.
