 ## Conventions
 
 - **Dates (v0.23):** show and accept dates as **DD-MM-YYYY** (except the dashboard's Today page, which writes them out: "Thursday 15th October", the year only when it isn't this year; Alan, 2026-10-09) (and times as 24-hour HH:MM) in everything Alan reads or types — messages, the dashboard, minutes and report text, the Excel export (cells formatted DD-MM-YYYY) and plain-English commands. **Store** dates as **YYYY-MM-DD** in the database, staging files, sources and settings, and **name files** `YYYY-MM-DD Title` so they sort in order. Convert at the edge; never mix the two in one place.
-- **Projects by name (BL-101):** a project is referred to by its **full name** in everything a person reads (the dashboard, reminders, printed lines, Word reports and their file names, drafts, ask creaite's replies). The short code appears **only** as the prefix of a work item's ID (`ABC-A-003`), where a code is defined or typed (Settings › Projects, the register, the Add project form, commands, filters, search; the dashboard's addresses keep it), where a machine matches on it (the register's signals, a `[CODE]` tag, an Outlook category, the **Draft email subject**), and in the command a reminder tells Alan to say ("Example Programme weekly report … — say weekly report ABC …"). `tracker.project_label(code)` (Python) and `pName(code)` (the dashboard) are the one place a name is looked up.
-- **VIP is private to Alan (BL-288):** never call or label a person a VIP, or say who is one, in anything creaite writes or may show or share: minutes, reports, the steerco one-pager, prep pages, drafts, proposed items, gists, the Excel export and replies. VIPs still work unlabelled (their alerts, first in Review, the early warning). The word stays only in the person's own VIP field, the register's VIP column and Settings › VIP alerts.
